  "title": "The density of a 2-dimensional minimizing cone is locally constant on its support away from the vertex",
  "statement": "Let P ∈ ℕ and let C ∈ 𝒟_2(ℝ^P) be minimizing in ℝ^P (IsMinimizingIn C univ), with ∂C = 0 (BoundaryVanishes C) and a cone (IsConeCurrent C). Then for every p ∈ spt C with p ≠ 0 there are δ > 0 and k ∈ ℕ such that HasMassDensity C y k (i.e. Θ²(μ_C, y) = k) for every y ∈ spt C ∩ B_δ(p).",
